   "reply": "The tests need three fixes in `money.py`: `split` must hand out the remainder cents instead of dropping them, `__str__` must handle negatives, and formatting should use integer arithmetic instead of floats. I'm rewriting the file with those changes.\n\n\n{\"action\": \"write\", \"path\": \"money.py\", \"content\": \"class Money:\\n    def __init__(self, cents):\\n        self.cents = cents\\n\\n    def __add__(self, o):\\n        return Money(self.cents + o.cents)\\n\\n    def __eq__(self, o):\\n        return isinstance(o, Money) and self.cents == o.cents\\n\\n    def __repr__(self):\\n        return f'Money({self.cents})'\\n\\n    def __str__(self):\\n        sign = '-' if self.cents < 0 else ''\\n        dollars, cents = divmod(abs(self.cents), 100)\\n        return f'{sign}${dollars:,}.{cents:02d}'\\n\\n    def split(self, n):\\n        if n < 1:\\n            raise ValueError('n must be at least 1')\\n        sign = -1 if self.cents < 0 else 1\\n        base, remainder = divmod(abs(self.cents), n)\\n        # Distribute the leftover cents one each to the first shares so the total is preserved.\\n        return [\\n            Money(sign * (base + 1 if i < remainder else base))\\n            for i in range(n)\\n        ]\\n\"}\n{\"action\": \"run\", \"args\": [\"-m\", \"unittest\", \"test_money\"]}",
